# Day's Undoing on Bot1's own turn: each player shuffles their hand and graveyard into their library and draws seven, then
# the turn ends (CR 724.1). Bot1's seven draws trigger Bot2's Orcish Bowmasters seven times, but those abilities
# triggered before the turn began to end, so they cease to exist and are never put on the stack (CR 724.1a; the card's
# ruling): Bot1 stays at 19 and the Orc Army keeps the one counter its enters trigger gave it. Day's Undoing is exiled,
# not shuffled in (it was on the stack) nor put into the graveyard (724.1b). Turn 4 is Bot2's.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Day's Undoing
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Orcish Bowmasters
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Orcish Bowmasters.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Target(Bot1)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Day's Undoing.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]
? ActivePlayer = Bot2

[Expect]
Turn = 4
Bot1.Life = 19
Bot2.Battlefield.Orc Army Token.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Hand.Count = 7
Exile = Day's Undoing
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
